    {
      "id": "crhjatf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Introduction to Life Processes"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Life processes include four core essential functions: Nutrition, Respiration, Transportation, and Excretion.",
        "Autotrophic nutrition synthesizes organic compounds using inorganic raw materials, while heterotrophic nutrition depends on consumed organic matter.",
        "Photosynthesis takes place in chloroplasts, converting solar energy into chemical energy stored as glucose.",
        "Human digestion involves mechanical breakdown and enzymatic digestion across the alimentary canal, completing in the small intestine.",
        "Respiration breaks down glucose to release energy in the form of ATP, occurring aerobically in mitochondria or anaerobically in cytoplasm.",
        "Plant transport involves Xylem for water/minerals (unidirectional) and Phloem for translocating sucrose (bidirectional)."
      ],
      "id": "ltmebl6"
    },
