    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dd438i1",
      "content": "Life processes are essential biological activities that maintain life. They include Nutrition, Respiration, Transportation and Excretion. These processes help organisms grow, obtain energy and remove wastes."
    },
    {
      "id": "94mgqjz",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "5159zp5",
      "src": "/books/Precis/RRB GS/images/image_5159zp5.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "id": "eidnv5r",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "ctlmhnb",
      "src": "/books/Precis/RRB GS/images/image_ctlmhnb.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "id": "e10g9r3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Nutrition"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xi3y63t",
      "content": "• Nutrition is the process of intake and utilization of food."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s8cq34i",
      "content": "• Provides energy and raw materials for growth."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d22dlr7",
      "content": "• Two main types: Autotrophic and Heterotrophic."
    },
    {
      "id": "v0gvtx5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Autotrophic & Heterotrophic Nutrition"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3twwppw",
      "content": "• Autotrophic Nutrition – Organisms prepare their own food (Plants)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0bsje4j",
      "content": "• Heterotrophic Nutrition – Organisms depend on others for food (Animals, Fungi)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "25uptfi",
      "content": "• Types of Heterotrophic: Saprophytic, Parasitic, Holozoic."
    },
    {
      "id": "ot9x2nz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Photosynthesis"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jk340ut",
      "content": "Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants prepare food using carbon dioxide and water in the presence of sunlight and chlorophyll."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ntqhho0",
      "content": "Equation: 6CO₂ + 6H₂O → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂ (in presence of sunlight &amp; chlorophyll)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "l6fa75s",
      "content": "• Factor: Sunlight"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "lggmgk9",
      "content": "• Factor: Chlorophyll"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "yhcdwjr",
      "content": "• Factor: Carbon dioxide"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "fak4khb",
      "content": "• Factor: Water"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4fobph0",
      "content": "• Factor: Temperature"
    },
    {
      "id": "w2uvt1k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Human Digestive System"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6d7esyp",
      "content": "• Mouth – Ingestion; Salivary amylase acts on starch."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zxkmhto",
      "content": "• Oesophagus – Food pipe; peristalsis movement."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1nxmkrq",
      "content": "• Stomach – HCl and Pepsin digest proteins."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "CHAPTER 5: LIFE PROCESSES",
      "id": "1jxznbe"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y7qdnwy",
      "content": "• Small Intestine – Digestion and absorption; bile &amp; pancreatic juice act."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mzce82y",
      "content": "• Large Intestine – Absorption of water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "al5acrl",
      "content": "• Rectum &amp; Anus – Egestion."
    },
    {
      "id": "q695s8i",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Respiration"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3wi45se",
      "content": "Respiration is the process of breakdown of food to release energy in the form of ATP."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mpifs4i",
      "content": "• Aerobic Respiration – In presence of oxygen; produces CO₂ and H₂O."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yd95zpe",
      "content": "• Anaerobic Respiration – In absence of oxygen; produces alcohol or lactic acid."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ogbj6m6",
      "content": "• Occurs in mitochondria."
    },
    {
      "id": "urh9c4c",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Human Respiratory System"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "slzmb8a",
      "content": "• Nose – Air filtration."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k8gfbu9",
      "content": "• Trachea – Windpipe."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g7wey3t",
      "content": "• Lungs – Site of gas exchange."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Autotrophic Nutrition",
        "Heterotrophic Nutrition"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Definition",
          "Organisms prepare their own food from simple inorganic materials",
          "Organisms depend on autotrophs or other organisms for organic food"
        ],
        [
          "Chlorophyll Requirement",
          "Essential for absorbing sunlight",
          "Not required"
        ],
        [
          "Examples",
          "Green plants, Cyanobacteria",
          "Animals, Fungi, Humans"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "qokpjac"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qleq4fs",
      "content": "• Alveoli – Increase surface area."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i09ffzf",
      "content": "• Diaphragm – Helps in breathing movement."
    },
    {
      "id": "71x9do2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Transportation in Humans"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f197jdq",
      "content": "• Heart pumps blood."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rzst1za",
      "content": "• Arteries carry blood away from heart."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vookmlw",
      "content": "• Veins carry blood to heart."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9xphjpq",
      "content": "• Capillaries allow exchange of substances."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7j8qlii",
      "content": "• Double circulation present."
    },
    {
      "id": "5t56zdp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Transportation in Plants"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yjef3gk",
      "content": "• Xylem transports water and minerals."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2ijfi68",
      "content": "• Phloem transports food."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kqn8aa4",
      "content": "• Transpiration helps in upward movement of water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wqle2fo",
      "content": "• Root pressure aids transport."
    },
    {
      "id": "2v2trda",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Excretion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t7uj89y",
      "content": "• Removal of metabolic waste products."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wzto83k",
      "content": "• Kidneys filter blood."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Complete digestion of carbohydrates, proteins, and fats occurs in the small intestine with the aid of pancreatic enzymes and bile juice.",
        "Aerobic respiration yields significantly higher ATP molecules in mitochondria than anaerobic respiration in cytoplasm/muscle cells.",
        "Xylem transport is unidirectional (root to leaves driven by transpiration pull), whereas Phloem translocation is bidirectional (source to sink)."
      ],
      "id": "7hqzsy5"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8csvbb8",
      "content": "• Nephron is functional unit of kidney."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aoos139",
      "content": "• Urea is major nitrogenous waste."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rhkn87s",
      "content": "• Urine stored in urinary bladder."
    },
    {
      "id": "laceeuf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "11. Quick Revision Points (RRB Focus)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6ao685m",
      "content": "1. Photosynthesis occurs in chloroplast."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zy51c15",
      "content": "2. Aerobic respiration produces more energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "le2z3ze",
      "content": "3. Small intestine is main site of absorption."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cczphtl",
      "content": "4. Xylem = Water transport; Phloem = Food transport."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3607m5q",
      "content": "5. Nephron is unit of kidney."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7shxi5g",
      "content": "6. Double circulation in humans."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
